{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>From the beginning of the sickle in the standing grain</b>. Its sense is: from when you begin to swing the sickle in the standing grain — for he has already mentioned when we begin to swing the sickle in the standing grain, in the context of the ʿomer, which is the first of our harvest. And its midrash (Sifrei 180) is to teach concerning the ʿomer that its reaping must be done only with a sickle."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:14:24.863658277Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}